  "summary": "Makes onSave async so it writes a JSON snapshot of the in-memory note store to data/notes.json after each save.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "Async onSave breaks the synchronous dispatch caller",
      "description": "The change makes onSave async, so dispatch in src/router.js:7 now returns a Promise for save actions. The server in src/main.js:9 passes that Promise straight to res.end, which accepts only a string or Buffer. Every POST /save request makes res.end throw a TypeError inside the request listener, which crashes the server. The writeFile promise also floats, so a failed write becomes an unhandled rejection. Make dispatch and the request handler await the result before calling res.end. Catch errors there and answer with a 500 status.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The change makes onSave async, so dispatch in src/router.js:7 now returns a Promise for save actions. The server in src/main.js:9 passes that Promise straight to res.end, which accepts only a string or Buffer.",
      "consequence": "Every POST /save request makes res.end throw a TypeError inside the request listener, which crashes the server. The writeFile promise also floats, so a failed write becomes an unhandled rejection.",
      "fix": "Make dispatch and the request handler await the result before calling res.end. Catch errors there and answer with a 500 status."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "file_path": "src/handlers.js",
      "line_number": 8,
      "line_end": 8,
      "title": "Snapshot write has no covering test",
      "description": "The change adds a file write and an async return to onSave. No test in the repository exercises onSave or the snapshot file. A test would have caught the crash in the save path. Future regressions in the snapshot write will also go unnoticed. Add a test that calls dispatch with the save action. The test should check the response text and the contents of the snapshot file.",
